<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17312" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex-tābesco</span></b> , bŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i>, <i>to pass away completely</i>, <i>to vanish</i>, <i>disappear.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: refugere oculi: corpus macie extabuit,
			Poët. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 3, 12, 26</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">is fame extabuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Galb. 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Thren. 4, 9</span></i>.—
			* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">videmus ceteras opiniones fictas atque vanas
					diuturnitate extabuisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 2, 2, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
